          <y:NodeLabel alignment="left" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="12" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="230.125" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="free" modelPosition="anywhere" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="271.59765625" x="6.8755772551145355" xml:space="preserve" y="7.192274018626904">The existing StudyField nodes refer to
the StudyField names - could be smart to
have these defined in a master definition
including resposne types and page references
where some can be for Other Trial Summary
Parameters of the various sub types.
In this way all Trial Summary Parameters 
get classified.

The 'Response Format' value then either the
data type for the response, or the CT codelist
name when a CT Term selection, or the
dictionary name when a Dictionary selection
for the related study field selection.

Maybe this must be a two step selection in UI.</y:NodeLabel>
